.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt KISSBUFD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kissbufd.conf
.Nd kissbufd configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr kissbufd 8
reads its settings from the file given with
.Fl c .
Options given on the command line override settings in the file.
.Pp
Each line holds one setting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
key = value
.Ed
.Pp
Whitespace around the key and the value is ignored.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
or
.Ql \&;
are ignored; an unquoted
.Ql #
that follows whitespace starts a trailing comment.
A value may be enclosed in double or single quotes to keep spaces or
.Ql # .
Unknown keys and invalid values are errors, reported with the file name
and line number.
If a key is given more than once, the last one wins.
.Pp
Boolean values are
.Cm yes ,
.Cm true ,
.Cm on ,
.Cm 1
or
.Cm no ,
.Cm false ,
.Cm off ,
.Cm 0 .
.Sh SETTINGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm device No = Ar path
TNC serial device.
Required, here or with
.Fl s .
.It Cm baud No = Ar speed
Serial speed: 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200 and,
where the system supports them, 230400, 460800, 500000, 921600, 1000000.
Default 57600.
.It Cm serial_mode No = Ar mode
Data bits (5 to 8), parity
.Pq Cm N , E , O
and stop bits (1 or 2), e.g.
.Cm 8N1 .
Default 8N1.
.It Cm dtr No = Ar bool
Assert DTR and RTS when opening the port.
Default yes.
.It Cm reopen_interval No = Ar seconds
Delay between attempts to reopen the serial port after the link is lost,
1 to 3600.
Default 2.
.It Cm buffer_size No = Ar bytes
TNC transmit buffer size in raw KISS bytes, 64 to 1048576.
Required, here or with
.Fl B .
.It Cm fill_percent No = Ar percent
Fill the TNC buffer up to this share of
.Cm buffer_size ,
1 to 100.
Frames larger than the resulting limit are dropped.
Default 95.
.It Cm ack_timeout No = Ar seconds
Time to wait for an ACKMODE ACK before a frame is considered lost and a
minor alarm is logged, 1 to 86400.
Default 60.
.It Cm queue_limit No = Ar bytes
Bytes of host frames held while waiting for room on the TNC, 1024 to
67108864.
Frames arriving while the queue is full are dropped.
Default 262144.
.It Cm pty_link No = Ar path
Create a symbolic link to the pseudo-terminal at
.Ar path .
Empty for none.
Default none.
.It Cm daemon No = Ar bool
Detach into the background, logging to syslog.
Default no.
Service files override this with
.Fl f
or
.Fl D .
.It Cm syslog No = Ar bool
Log to syslog (facility daemon) instead of standard error.
Default no.
.It Cm pidfile No = Ar path
Write the process ID to
.Ar path .
Empty for none.
Default none.
.It Cm verbose No = Ar level
0 for warnings and notices, 1 for informational messages, 2 for
per-frame debug output.
Default 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa @SYSCONFDIR@/kissbufd/*.conf
configuration files used by the service files
.It Pa @DOCDIR@/kissbufd.conf.sample
annotated sample
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# @SYSCONFDIR@/kissbufd/tnc0.conf
device      = /dev/serial/by-id/usb-<your-tnc>-if00
baud        = 57600
buffer_size = 32768
pty_link    = @RUNDIR@/kissbufd/tnc0
verbose     = 1
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kissbufd 8
